{
  "svet": {
    "id": "world",
    "name": "World",
    "country": "svet",
    "osm_name": "World",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "bbox": [-180, -85.05, 180, 85.05],
    "note": "The base world map from its own pipeline (world-map.yml). `osmfr` is deliberately ABSENT: it's built not from a regional PBF but from OSM coastlines, Natural Earth and the Geofabrik index (workers/world/sources.py). `admin_level: 2` means the package sits on Drive directly in `svet/`, with no region level."
  },
  "svet_basic": {
    "id": "world_basic",
    "name": "World – basic",
    "country": "svet_basic",
    "osm_name": "World",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "bbox": [-180, -85.05, 180, 85.05],
    "note": "The world map in its `basic` form – state borders and download regions only, no water or lakes (input `variant` in world-map.yml, lookup workers/data/world-variants.json). ITS OWN KEY, not a suffix to `svet`, by rule 2 of CLAUDE.md: a name is a promise about extent, so `basic` must not land on `svet.zip` or its node in `maps.json` – whoever downloads “the world map” from the catalog must not get a map without seas. So `country` is `svet_basic` too: the package sits in its own Drive folder and is its own root node in the catalog, beside `svet`."
  },
  "svet_ground": {
    "id": "world_ground",
    "name": "World – ground",
    "country": "svet_ground",
    "osm_name": "World",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "bbox": [-180, -85.05, 180, 85.05],
    "note": "The world map in its `ground` form – sea, lakes, state borders and their names, no download regions (input `variant` in world-map.yml). Its own key for the reason `svet_basic` has one. The app bundles it as the ground of a map with nothing to draw."
  },
  "navigacia_slovensko": {
    "id": "navigation_slovakia",
    "name": "Navigation – Slovakia",
    "country": "navigacia_slovensko",
    "osm_name": "Slovensko",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "bbox": [16.83, 47.73, 22.57, 49.61],
    "note": "The routing GRAPH (Valhalla), not a map – `navigation.yml`, extent from workers/data/routing-areas.json. `osmfr` is deliberately ABSENT: `workers/routing/pbf.sh` downloads the PBF by that lookup, since the graph's extent is another question than the map's – the graph is NOT split by region (see there). `admin_level: 2` means the package sits on Drive directly in `navigacia_slovensko/`, with no region level. And `country` EQUALS the key – not a shared `navigacia` for every scope: `admin_level: 2` makes the country a catalog node too, so two scopes under one `navigacia` would OVERWRITE each other's item (both packages on Drive, the catalog knowing the second). The same decision for the same reason as `svet_basic`."
  },
  "navigacia_slovensko_susedia": {
    "id": "navigation_slovakia_neighbours",
    "name": "Navigation – Slovakia and neighbours",
    "country": "navigacia_slovensko_susedia",
    "osm_name": "Slovensko + CZ, AT, HU, PL, UA",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "bbox": [9.47, 45.38, 40.23, 55.05],
    "note": "The same as `navigacia_slovensko`, with a graph across borders – without it one can't drive to Austria, so neither avoid lacking a vignette there. ITS OWN KEY, not a suffix (rule 2): whoever downloads `navigacia_slovensko` from the catalog must not get a graph that ends at the border – nor the reverse. Its own `country` (and so its own catalog node) for the same reason as `navigacia_slovensko`."
  },
  "slovensko": {
    "id": "slovakia",
    "name": "Slovakia",
    "country": "slovensko",
    "osm_name": "Slovensko",
    "admin_level": 2,
    "iso": "SK",
    "routing_area": "slovensko",
    "bbox": [16.815, 47.71, 22.585, 49.635],
    "osmfr": { "dir": "europe", "slugs": ["slovakia-latest"] },
    "note": "All of Slovakia as one region – and the PARENT of its regions: each has `osmfr.parent: slovensko` and `workers/plan/pbf.sh` cuts it out of this file (`osmium extract -s smart`). osm.fr's ready `{region}-latest.osm.pbf` is NOT USED – it isn't referentially complete, so an area reaching into a neighbouring region (CHKO Malé Karpaty, CHKO Záhorie, the Záhorie forests) lacks members and Planetiler drops it WHOLE, the in-region part too. Measured, with figures in the pbf.sh header. `iso` is the two-letter country code, here for ROUTING: an archive edge carries its country, or the vignette has nothing to stand on (`workers/data/vignettes.json`). Regions take it through their `country`, so it's written once. `routing_area` is the key in `workers/data/routing-areas.json` the CCH NODE ORDER is computed over – every region of a country must stand on the same one, or their archives must not be joined on the phone."
  },
